<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:31Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-sports" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-8171?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Bundesliga season 2026-27: All you need to know</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab4a61987b51fb28da8de696045be881ce9d1adf60c969c2e5af6fe35350f015</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:31Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T06:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bundesliga-season-2026-27-all-you-need-to-know/a-78061925--7d4b7d525a5e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bundesliga-season-2026-27-all-you-need-to-know/a-78061925?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From key dates to rising football stars and changes, DW has the latest on the new Bundesliga season.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Schalke coach looks to Bosnia bond in Bundesliga return</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6afd1faa670b6f691815408267fe965bcc0e624d5d1b11b2b4a631016f884e3</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:31Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T14:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/schalke-coach-looks-to-bosnia-bond-in-bundesliga-return/a-78486008--8e159c49e970.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/schalke-coach-looks-to-bosnia-bond-in-bundesliga-return/a-78486008?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After three seasons in the second division, Schalke are back in the Bundesliga. Just a year ago, few would have guessed that their revival would largely be 'Made in Bosnia.'</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>The new Bundesliga season is here, but has the glow gone?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76fb767ab323116e82279d7805b591e0c479c4c258c72b6511ef88a26bb63322</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:31Z</updated><published>2026-08-24T14:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-new-bundesliga-season-is-here-but-has-the-glow-gone/a-78062032--252bbbfe7518.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-new-bundesliga-season-is-here-but-has-the-glow-gone/a-78062032?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Another Bundesliga season arrives, but are the golden years of Germany's top football league already over, and what can it do to change its course?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Bernadette Amani 'living her dream' at Bayern Munich</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9041a09c8fb0cb3401644243d023f22b0dc414f83cadb7238b779d3fbf43a57</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:31Z</updated><published>2026-08-20T08:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bernadette-amani-living-her-dream-at-bayern-munich/a-78141213--a7b3f72617e6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bernadette-amani-living-her-dream-at-bayern-munich/a-78141213?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bernadette Amani is heading into her first full season with Bayern Munich, having joined the club in January. Making a living at football is something she never imagined possible while growing up in rural Ivory Coast.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Andre Rankel named Germany's new men's ice hockey coach</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dcb491a55807e99c7479e1a54f50da013fe3a3ec4cf6b43fd1181faa2a31660d</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:31Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T14:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/andre-rankel-named-germany-s-new-men-s-ice-hockey-coach/a-78532470--5960c1ee95d4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/andre-rankel-named-germany-s-new-men-s-ice-hockey-coach/a-78532470?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's men's ice hockey team has appointed a new head coach following a string of dissappointing tournaments. He's two decades younger than the man he's replacing but he has no previous experience as a head coach.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>New study shows German football remains male-dominated</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5d2e59d5fe1099cdd00c6fe37421459febd4fda9cf7023737846b267ded4d2e</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:31Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T13:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-study-shows-german-football-remains-male-dominated/a-78532569--8c6ff2b85328.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-study-shows-german-football-remains-male-dominated/a-78532569?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The top leagues of German football remain a largely male environment. A new study reveals that only seven clubs have women in upper management levels.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Venus' US Open invitation raises questions about wild cards</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3bfc44a1e379abef9bd5518e6f18ebf01d66aa998ac6989a0bac9afa90a652cb</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:31Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T12:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/venus-us-open-invitation-raises-questions-about-wild-cards/a-78524056--418fc356bf81.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/venus-us-open-invitation-raises-questions-about-wild-cards/a-78524056?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Although her current world ranking wouldn't allow it, Venus Williams is set to play singles in the US Open – thanks to a wild card. Who gets these coveted spots—and how?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Sydney Marathon medal wrongly shows German landmark</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8d98d810f6d4c216c1a13079fa5adbf0ef902c130847e01a1711a42f6927f3cc</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:31Z</updated><published>2026-08-23T06:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sydney-marathon-medal-wrongly-shows-german-landmark/a-78473705--b50f29aa4396.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sydney-marathon-medal-wrongly-shows-german-landmark/a-78473705?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A medal minted for finishers in the Sydney Marathon features a skyline of the city — with one landmark from rather far away. Organizers say the muddle only makes the medal "a little more unique."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ronaldinho to make football comeback aged 46</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1adc3784684d8fe01a31bd7ba974236ca78abfd8de9856c80a189eb8ebf7b852</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:31Z</updated><published>2026-08-21T08:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ronaldinho-to-make-football-comeback-aged-46/a-78453950--f9e1ae697006.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ronaldinho-to-make-football-comeback-aged-46/a-78453950?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More than a decade after his last professional appearance, Brazilian superstar Ronaldinho is set for a comeback. The former world player of the year is to play in Italy’s third tier.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Amanal Petros: From refugee to European champion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff9dc7eddb69608de8981ad9c369e750d73bd983f37988145b5056c93859c6c2</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:31Z</updated><published>2026-08-19T11:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/amanal-petros-from-refugee-to-european-champion/a-78428504--7568f015ebdb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/amanal-petros-from-refugee-to-european-champion/a-78428504?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Amanal Petros fled the Eritrean–Ethiopian war and came to Germany as a teenager. Now one of the world's top marathon runners, he recently won gold at the European Athletics Championships.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>UEFA, other football federations unite against Infantino</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:030ebf4fcf3181e2033b775e54e5c80cb33fa25c9c2fa6b6dabb67a2cd463625</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:31Z</updated><published>2026-08-10T11:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uefa-other-football-federations-unite-against-infantino/a-78301601--0e6c3356b96f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uefa-other-football-federations-unite-against-infantino/a-78301601?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A few weeks ago, Gianni Infantino looked set for another unopposed term as FIFA president. Now, with an election looming, the beleagured football executive is counting the numbers and could be hanging by a thread.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>How Gianni Infantino rose to rule football</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bdecc3a2711e321ef8617572a4be568de6c56805850ff51101b6fa511fe75f08</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:31Z</updated><published>2026-08-06T12:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-gianni-infantino-rose-to-rule-football/a-78242568--63c1ed54d01d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-gianni-infantino-rose-to-rule-football/a-78242568?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Gianni Infantino is staying on as FIFA president despite growing pressure to step down. So who is football's most powerful man, why did UEFA and others turn against him, and how did he reassert his authority?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Spain won the World Cup, but Donald Trump 'cast a shadow'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:33bc1a7821f24589c34febd3736efdb93d4365e78baf56903d8c9e4f1cba37c1</id><updated>2026-08-30T15:57:31Z</updated><published>2026-07-20T13:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-won-the-world-cup-but-donald-trump-cast-a-shadow/a-78037668--06a5f9e114ce.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-won-the-world-cup-but-donald-trump-cast-a-shadow/a-78037668?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Though Donald Trump mostly stayed clear of stadiums, the World Cup may influence the US midterm elections. DW looks at the political implications of "the most successful sporting event maybe in the history of the world."</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry></feed>
